  "title": "Literature Review: Transformer Attention Nlp",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "This survey covers recent work on transformer attention nlp, drawing from 15 papers.",
      "citations": [],
      "verification_statuses": [],
      "supporting_claim_ids": [],
      "nli_score": null,
      "hallucination_rate": 0.0,
      "support_rate": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "We propose a new simple network architecture, the Transformer, based solely on attention mechanisms, dispensing with recurrence and convolutions entirely.",
      "citations": [
        "8f8686ea-bbc1-56db-8744-329c88a02e37"
      ],
      "verification_statuses": [
        "unverifiable"
      ],
      "supporting_claim_ids": [
        "e8de2033-16bb-5b58-a7bb-b9c12dd199c1"
      ],
      "nli_score": null,
      "hallucination_rate": 0.0,
      "support_rate": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Most recent analysis has focused on model outputs (e.g., language model surprisal) or internal vector representations (e.g., probing classifiers).Complementary to these works, we propose methods for analyzing the attention mechanisms of pre-trained models and apply them to BERT.BERT's attention heads exhibit patterns such as attending to delimiter tokens, specific positional offsets, or broadly attending over the whole sentence, with heads in the same layer often exhibiting similar behaviors.",
      "citations": [
        "5786404d-077c-5aa6-809c-60e0376179dc"
      ],
      "verification_statuses": [
        "unverifiable"
      ],
      "supporting_claim_ids": [
        "fb65228e-323b-5054-a02f-6465a6fb740f"
      ],
      "nli_score": null,
      "hallucination_rate": 0.0,
      "support_rate": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "We propose a taxonomy of attention models according to four dimensions: the representation of the input, the compatibility function, the distribution function, and the multiplicity of the input and/or output.",
      "citations": [
        "d6971e48-ce6a-5ffa-8c52-4057044c6555"
      ],
      "verification_statuses": [
        "unverifiable"
      ],
      "supporting_claim_ids": [
        "2d5899a5-cdda-5f53-bf5d-e4ab94e93342"
      ],
      "nli_score": null,
      "hallucination_rate": 0.0,
      "support_rate": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Our model achieves 41.8 BLEU.",
      "citations": [
        "8f8686ea-bbc1-56db-8744-329c88a02e37"
      ],
      "verification_statuses": [
        "unverifiable"
      ],
      "supporting_claim_ids": [
        "ba967108-ab25-57f3-a3b0-6022f88d33ab"
      ],
      "nli_score": null,
      "hallucination_rate": 0.0,
      "support_rate": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The dominant sequence transduction models are based on complex recurrent or convolutional neural networks in an encoder-decoder configuration.",
      "citations": [
        "8f8686ea-bbc1-56db-8744-329c88a02e37"
      ],
      "verification_statuses": [
        "unverifiable"
      ],
      "supporting_claim_ids": [
        "38d29487-f8bf-5790-8c79-c161699b4935"
      ],
      "nli_score": null,
      "hallucination_rate": 0.0,
      "support_rate": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The best performing models also connect the encoder and decoder through an attention mechanism.",
      "citations": [
        "8f8686ea-bbc1-56db-8744-329c88a02e37"
      ],
      "verification_statuses": [
        "unverifiable"
      ],
      "supporting_claim_ids": [
        "01f084c9-9d0b-58a7-9d6d-b8d7e9216965"
      ],
      "nli_score": null,
      "hallucination_rate": 0.0,
      "support_rate": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "We show that well configured Transformer models outperform our baseline models based on the shallow stack of LSTM recurrent neural network layers.",
      "citations": [
        "7d5b0df1-2f41-54ff-909b-f06c4a4c453d"
      ],
      "verification_statuses": [
        "unverifiable"
      ],
      "supporting_claim_ids": [
        "e677a5ad-1a1d-5c36-8c8a-a5b2a673902f"
      ],
      "nli_score": null,
      "hallucination_rate": 0.0,
      "support_rate": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "A noted limitation: In this work, we address the challenging task of referring segmentation.",
      "citations": [
        "42491378-1f5b-5cd5-a3e6-4bc72a8084ab"
      ],
      "verification_statuses": [
        "unverifiable"
      ],
      "supporting_claim_ids": [
        "e480f162-c213-52b5-bc96-5cfa1efb2333"
      ],
      "nli_score": null,
      "hallucination_rate": 0.0,
      "support_rate": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "A noted limitation: Second, we show that deep Transformer language models do not require positional encoding.",
      "citations": [
        "7d5b0df1-2f41-54ff-909b-f06c4a4c453d"
      ],
      "verification_statuses": [
        "unverifiable"
      ],
      "supporting_claim_ids": [
